menu "USB Ethernet (usb_dev_ethernet)"

    choice USBNET_CLASS
        prompt "USB Ethernet device class"
        default USBNET_CLASS_NCM
        help
            Which USB communications class the device presents for the
            USB Ethernet link (192.168.7.1).

            CDC-NCM is the default: it is the class Windows ships an
            in-box driver for (UsbNcm.sys — Windows 11 24H2 removed the
            legacy RNDIS driver), and macOS/Linux support it natively.
            The device class implementation is WiCAN-authored (vendored
            components/cherryusb fork; upstream CherryUSB has none).

            RNDIS remains for old Windows 10 hosts; CDC-ECM for
            macOS/Linux-only deployments (Windows has NO in-box ECM
            driver — bench-verified on Win11 26200).

        config USBNET_CLASS_NCM
            bool "CDC-NCM (Windows 11 / macOS / Linux in-box)"

        config USBNET_CLASS_RNDIS
            bool "RNDIS (legacy Windows 10; removed in Windows 11 24H2)"

        config USBNET_CLASS_ECM
            bool "CDC-ECM (macOS / Linux; NOT Windows)"

    endchoice

endmenu
